{"tool_name":"aeon.py","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"aeon.py","home":"https://github.com/sybila/biodivine-aeon-py","license":"MIT","summary":"AEON is a Python framework (with Rust backend) for analysis of Boolean networks. It supports a wide range of techniques: (1) Loading/storing networks from SBML-qual, .bnet and .aeon format. (2) Support for partially specified networks with uncertain dynamics. (3) Attractor computation and bifurcation analysis. (4) Model checking and property classification based on (H)CTL. (5) Control and reprogramming using one step/permanent/temporary perturbations.\n\nYou can learn more about the usage of AEON in the \"examples\" folder of the git repository.","addition_date":"2022-11-06T12:28:50.395182Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:37:12.153820Z","tool_type":["Library"],"version":["0.1.1","0.2.0","0.3.0"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:aeon.py","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"safranek@fi.muni.cz","name":"David \u0160afr\u00e1nek","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"xbenes3@fi.muni.cz","name":"Nikola Bene\u0161","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"xpastva@fi.muni.cz","name":"Samuel Pastva","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"maturity":"Mature","name":"AEON.py","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"daemontus","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btac624","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: AEON.py is a Python library for the analysis of the long-term behaviour in very large asynchronous Boolean networks. It provides significant computational improvements over the state-of-the-art methods for attract- or detection. Furthermore, it admits the analysis of partially specified Boolean networks with uncertain update functions. It also includes techniques for identifying viable source-target control strategies and the assessment of their robustness with respect to parameter perturbations.","authors":[{"name":"Benes N."},{"name":"Brim L."},{"name":"Huvar O."},{"name":"Pastva S."},{"name":"Safranek D."},{"name":"Smijakova E."}],"citationCount":9,"date":"2022-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"AEON.py: Python library for attractor analysis in asynchronous Boolean networks"},"pmid":"36102786"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"AEON.py","home":"https://bio.tools/aeon.py","license":"MIT","version":["0.1.1","0.2.0","0.3.0"],"summary":"AEON is a Python framework (with Rust backend) for analysis of Boolean networks. It supports a wide range of techniques: (1) Loading/storing networks from SBML-qual, .bnet and .aeon format. (2) Support for partially specified networks with uncertain dynamics. (3) Attractor computation and bifurcation analysis. (4) Model checking and property classification based on (H)CTL. (5) Control and reprogramming using one step/permanent/temporary perturbations.\n\nYou can learn more about the usage of AEON in the \"examples\" folder of the git repository.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:aeon.py/lib/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":12,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":2,"year":"2024"},{"count":4,"year":"2025"},{"count":4,"year":"2026"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btac624","pmid":"36102786","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"AEON.py: Python library for attractor analysis in asynchronous Boolean networks.","year":2022}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":true,"copyright":false,"https":true